# It's a Wired World after All: Children, Books, and the Internet.

**Authors:** Skurzynski, Gloria

## Abstract
Discusses the advantages of computer technology and digital communication in literacy and literacy education, cautioning that printed books should never be abandoned in favor of digital communication despite its advantages. Examines how digital communication can be used to promote literacy for poor and isolated children in all parts of the world. (SM)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ594246

